# The bundle is built on Windows and graded in a Linux container. Without this,
# git's autocrlf rewrites shipped scripts to CRLF on checkout and the Delivery
# Gate rejects the entrypoint (PF4.crlf_repaired_script).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# The vendored verifier engine ships exactly as it arrived, CRLF and all: the
# client computes a Layer 0 hash from these .py files directly, so normalising
# them would change the bytes it fingerprints. Left untouched on purpose.
*/tests/rl_world_verifiers/** -text
